    {
      "id": "concept-principle-of-explosion-logic-joke",
      "kind": "concept",
      "promptEs": "principio de explosión · P∧¬P",
      "answerEn": "In classical logic, accepting both a claim and its negation makes it possible to derive any claim.",
      "noteEn": "P∧¬P represents a proposition P together with ‘not P,’ a direct contradiction. The principle is called explosion because unrestricted conclusions then follow. The joke treats those conclusions as a way to obtain unrelated personal facts and plans rather than merely proving propositions.",
      "tags": ["concept", "logic", "contradiction", "joke"]
    }
